      "independent_solution": "The whole graph is {(t,4-(2/3)t): t is real}, not a segment. Its only axis points are (0,4) and (6,0). For x<0, y>4 and the point is in II; for 0<x<6, 0<y<4 and it is in I; for x>6, y<0 and it is in IV. The boundary points lie on the axes and in no quadrant. If x<0 and y<0, then 2x+3y<0, so III is impossible. (-3,6), (3,2), and (9,-2) witness the other three quadrants. The origin is not on the graph.",
